---
// Loads the <img-comparison-slider> web component. Rendered by BlogPost.astro only on
// posts whose body uses the element, so other pages don't download it. Usage in a post:
//
// <img-comparison-slider aria-label="Drag to compare A and B">
//   <figure slot="first" class="compare-pane"><img src="..." alt="..."><figcaption>A</figcaption></figure>
//   <figure slot="second" class="compare-pane"><img src="..." alt="..."><figcaption>B</figcaption></figure>
// </img-comparison-slider>
//
// Styles live in src/styles/components/compare-slider.css. The library's own stylesheet is
// deliberately NOT imported: it hides the whole element until the script runs, so a reader
// without JavaScript would see nothing. Ours shows the first image instead.
---

<script>
	import "img-comparison-slider";
</script>
